[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"732","stub":{"id":"732","section":"3. New Bridge Road to Moore Road, Richardsmere","altname":"Lower Octoraro","river":"Octoraro Creek","difficulty":"II","states":["USA-MRY"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"74","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"On weekends, it seems to be OK to park in the bus turnaround area on the downstream River right side of the bridge.  But there's only room for 2 or 3 cars here, so try to leave as few cars here as possible.  On weekdays, the bus turnaround is needed for school buses to turn around so however inviting it might seem, this area must be kept clear.  Look around, there may be other options.","id":"107183","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Horseshoe Road Bridge Put-in","distance":"0","photoID":"0","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"Take out on Moore Road on River right above the US 222 bridge in the historic mill town of Richardsmere.","id":"107188","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Moore Rd. Richardsmere Take-out","distance":"6.1","photoID":"0","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"If you have a large group, there is more parking at the Ballfield at River left just below the US 222 bridge","id":"107189","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Ballfield Take-out","distance":"6.15","photoID":"0","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"891344","ext":"jpg","post_id":"895241","description":null,"caption":" on Octoraro Creek @New Bridge Road to Richardsmere","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/891344","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/891344"}},{"id":"1266","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3752","description":"This dam can form a great hole at high levels, and a big wave at flood stage.  It is located 200 yards above the Route 1 bridge in Cecil County.","caption":"New River Ranch Falls","poi_name":"The Falls","subject":"Falls","author":"Walt Shank","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1266","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1266"}}],"detail":{"id":"732","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"Nice little section with some trashy and scenic surroundings. This is a kind of a forgotten corner of MD, but it's worth visiting and the river is worth running. It's kind of like the Brandywine without any dams.\n\nThe first 2.6 miles are pretty mellow, but things start to get going after the Rt. 1 bridge. Fun Class II rapids result as the Octoraro (which is Native American for \"rushing waters\") drops down to the Susquehanna below Conowingo Dam. Take out on a small side road before the Rt. 222 bridge in the historic mill town of Richardsmere.\n\nThe [Upper Octoraro](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/3562/) is categorized as a Pennsylvania stream.","averageGradient":"15","maxGradient":"30","length":"6.2","correlations":[{"reachID":"732","isPrimary":false,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"levelFT","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"2.4","beginMediumRunnable":"2.6","beginHighRunnable":"6","endHighRunnable":"9"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"Brandywine Creek at Chadds Ford, PA","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"01481000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"175","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value